#. type: Title ==
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:10
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "How is GBIF-mediated data used?"
msgstr "GBIF 所提供的資料是如何被運用的？"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:16
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:13
msgid "Both data availability and data use have increased over time."
msgstr "隨著時間，資料的可取得性與使用率均有所提升。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:17
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:14
msgid "Data integration facilitates global research and access."
msgstr "資料整合有助於全球研究與資料存取。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:18
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:15
msgid "Uses of GBIF-mediated data span disciplinary boundaries."
msgstr "GBIF 所提供的資料應用範圍跨越了學科界限。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:19
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:16
msgid "The scientific areas using GBIF-mediated data are conceptually diverse and change in prevalence over time."
msgstr "各科學領域使用GBIF所提供之資料的概念各不相同，且其普及程度會隨時間而變化。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:20
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:17
msgid "Globally integrated datasets enable researchers to ask both basic and applied questions at taxonomic, temporal and spatial scales that would be otherwise impossible."
msgstr "全球整合的資料集使研究人員能夠在分類學、時間與空間層面上探討基礎與應用層面的問題，而若無此類資料集，這些研究將難以實現。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:21
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:18
msgid "The synergistic roles of observation- and specimen-based biodiversity data highlight the value and need for deeper integration with phylogenetic, environmental, phenotypic, ecological and genetic sources of data."
msgstr "基於觀察與標本的生物多樣性資料所展現的協同作用，凸顯了將這些資料與系統發生學、環境、表型、生態及遺傳等資料來源進行更深入整合的價值與必要性。"

#. type: Block title
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:23
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structural topic model results from 4,035 studies that used GBIF-mediated data published between 2003 and 2019."
msgstr "依據 2003 年至 2019 年間發表、使用 GBIF 提供的資料的 4,035 項研究所得出的結構性主題模型結果。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:28
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:25
msgid "GBIF-mediated data is also used for monitoring the state of biodiversity and progress towards achieving the targets of the Convention on Biological Diversity.  The increase in availability of GBIF occurrence data is one of the indicators for tracking progress towards the achievement of Aichi Biodiversity target 19 and GBIF is a key data source in the creation of a number of other indicators, including the https://www.bipindicators.net/indicators/species-status-information-index[Species Status Information Index^], https://www.bipindicators.net/indicators/species-habitat-index[Species Habitat Index^] and the https://www.bipindicators.net/indicators/biodiversity-habitat-index[Biodiversity Habitat Index^]."
msgstr "透過 GBIF 提供的資料，亦用於監測生物多樣性的現況，以及在實現生物多樣性公約目標方面的進展。  提升 GBIF 分布資料的可用性，是追蹤實現愛知生物多樣性目標 19 進展的指標之一；此外，GBIF 也是建立多項其他指標的關鍵資料來源，包括https://www.bipindicators.net/indicators/species-status-information-index[物種狀態資訊指數^]、 https://www.bipindicators.net/indicators/species-habitat-index[物種棲地指數^] 以及 https://www.bipindicators.net/indicators/biodiversity-habitat-index[生物多樣性棲地指數^]。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:31
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:28
msgid "While the utility of GBIF-mediated data is clear, the wide variety of sources of data accessible through GBIF, spanning museum collections, citizen science, metagenomics, among others, means that not all GBIF-mediated data will be fit for every use.  Key components of using GBIF-mediated data are understanding how to access the specific data that you need from what is available in GBIF and understanding some of the common data quality issues that affect the data so as to facilitate processing of the data before analysis."
msgstr "雖然透過 GBIF 提供的資料具有明確價值，但由於可透過 GBIF 存取的資料來源種類繁多，涵蓋博物館館藏、公民科學、總體基因學等領域，這意味著並非所有透過 GBIF 獲取的資料都適合每種用途。  使用 GBIF提供資料的關鍵在於：了解如何從 GBIF 現有資源中取得所需的特定資料，並掌握影響資料品質的常見問題，以便在分析前對資料進行預處理。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:40
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "*What is available to me?*\n"
msgstr "*我能獲得哪些服務？*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:42
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:44
msgid "Through the search functions on the website, users can access data that can either be directly downloaded through GBIF or accessed from the original sources following links that GBIF provides."
msgstr "透過網站上的搜尋功能，使用者可以取得相關資料，這些資料既可直接透過 GBIF 下載，也可透過 GBIF 提供的連結從原始來源取得。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:44
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:46
msgid "Remember that as a data user you should read and agree with the terms of the GBIF https://www.gbif.org/terms/data-user[Data User Agreement^] that include https://www.gbif.org/citation-guidelines[correctly citing^] the use of GBIF-mediated data."
msgstr "請記住，身為資料使用者，您應閱讀並同意 GBIF https://www.gbif.org/terms/data-user[資料使用者協議^] 的條款，其中包含 https://www.gbif.org/citation-guidelines[正確引用^] 透過 GBIF 取得之資料的使用規範。"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:48
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:50
msgid "The data available to you are:"
msgstr "您可取用的資料如下："

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:50
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:52
msgid "Primary biodiversity data - occurrence, checklist and sampling event data that is provided to users through the one of the 3 download formats:"
msgstr "基本生物多樣性資料，包括物種出現紀錄、物種清單及採樣活動資料，這些資料將透過以下3種下載格式之一提供給使用者："

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:51
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Simple*: https://www.gbif.org/faq?question=csv-download[Tab delimited CSV^]. Only contains the data after GBIF interpretation. No multimedia included. \n"
msgstr "*簡單版*：https://www.gbif.org/faq?question=csv-download[以制表符分隔的 CSV 檔案^]。僅包含經 GBIF 解析後的資料。不含多媒體內容。 \n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:52
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Darwin Core Archive*: The https://www.gbif.org/faq?question=dwc-download[Darwin Core Archive^] (DwC-A) contains both the original data as the publisher provided it and the GBIF interpretation. Links (but not files) to multimedia included.\n"
msgstr "*達爾文核心檔案集*：https://www.gbif.org/faq?question=dwc-download[達爾文核心檔案集^]（DwC-A）同時包含發佈者提供的原始資料，以及 GBIF 的解析結果。其中包含多媒體內容的連結（但不包含檔案本身）。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:53
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Species list*: Tab delimited CSV with the distinct list of names in the search result and as a map visualization of the data.\n"
msgstr "*物種清單*：以制表符分隔的 CSV 檔案，其中包含搜尋結果中各物種名稱的獨特清單，並以地圖形式將資料視覺化呈現。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:54
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "A range of metrics are provided for https://www.gbif.org/analytics/global[countries and regions^], data publishers, datasets and data searches that provide taxonomic breakdowns, trends in data collection and highlight data quality issues. For countries, these metrics can be also be downloaded in the form of a PDF activity report. \n"
msgstr "我們提供一系列指標 https://www.gbif.org/analytics/global[國家和區域^]，涵蓋資料發布者、資料集和資料搜索，這些指標提供分類細項、資料收集趨勢並凸顯資料品質問題。對於各國，這些指標也可以 PDF 活動報告的形式下載\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:55
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "https://www.gbif.org/resource/search?contentType=literature&literatureType=journal&relevance=GBIF_USED&peerReview=true[Searchable database of publications^] that have used GBIF-mediated data.\n"
msgstr "https://www.gbif.org/resource/search?contentType=literature&literatureType=journal&relevance=GBIF_USED&peerReview=true[可搜尋的文獻資料庫^]，收錄了曾使用 GBIF 提供之資料的出版物。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/using-gbif-mediated-data.adoc:56
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:60
msgid "Searches can be performed on the https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/search?occurrence_status=present&q=[occurrences^], https://www.gbif.org/species/search?q=[species^], https://www.gbif.org/dataset/search?q=[datasets^], https://www.gbif.org/publisher/search?q=[publishers] and https://www.gbif.org/resource/search?q=[resources^], and each search function carries a set of filters that allow for more refined searching and additional data associated with the data, for example, https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/gallery?occurrence_status=present[images^], can be found in tabs associated with the search."
msgstr "可於 https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/search?occurrence_status=present&q=[出現紀錄^]、https://www.gbif.org/species/search?q=[物種^]、 https://www.gbif.org/dataset/search?q=[資料集^]、 https://www.gbif.org/publisher/search?q=[發布者] 以及 https://www.gbif.org/resource/search?q=[資源^] 進行搜尋，每個搜尋功能皆附有一組篩選器，可進行更精確的搜尋，並檢視與資料相關的附加資訊，例如， https://www.gbif.org/occurrence/gallery?occurrence_status=present[images^]，這些篩選條件皆可於搜尋相關的分頁中找到。"

#. type: Title ==
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:1
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/description.adoc:14
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/solutions.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data access"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:6
msgid "In this module, you will learn how GBIF's data is used and accessed.  You will also learn about the handling of data quality and GBIF's data quality flags."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:11
msgid "The GBIF https://www.gbif.org/literature-tracking[literature tracking system^] has identified over 5,000 uses of GBIF mediated data, most of which are in peer-reviewed articles.  The majority of these uses are in the field of ecology, but others relate to climate change, conservation, human health and agriculture.  A systematic review of the use of https://www.gbif.org/news/4tJNXqSLYd37InZxyPrU7E/data-integration-enables-global-biodiversity-synthesis[GBIF-mediated data by Heberling et al. (2020)^] showed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "intro-to-gbif::fig3.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Accessing GBIF-mediated data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:32
msgid "There are three points of access to GBIF-mediated data: http://www.gbif.org[GBIF.org^], the https://www.gbif.org/developer/summary[Application Programming Interface (API) services^], and https://www.gbif.org/occurrence-snapshots[cloud-based datasets^]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:34
msgid "Using the website requires no programming experience and allows for quick and easy search, filter and download functions for GBIF-mediated data, as well as a range of additional tools and metrics that are not available through API services."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:36
msgid "API services allow continued access to GBIF-mediated data through other systems and can be the basis for the development of tools that allow for the interrogation of the data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:38
msgid "Examples include https://www.gbif.org/tool/81747/rgbif[rgbif^], https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/CoordinateCleaner/versions/2.0-18[CoordinateCleaner^], and https://www.gbif.org/tool/OlyoYyRbKCSCkMKIi4oIT/pygbif-gbif-python-client[pygbif^], as well as, specialized tools that allow for more specific use cases, such as http://geocat.kew.org/[GeoCat^] for Red List assessments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:40
msgid "With regards to cloud-based datasets, GBIF makes data available on the https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/dataset/gbif[Microsoft Planetary Computer (Azure)^], as an https://registry.opendata.aws/gbif/[Amazon AWS Open Dataset^] and on a public https://console.cloud.google.com/storage/browser/public-datasets-gbif[Google GCS bucket^] and https://console.cloud.google.com/marketplace/product/bigquery-public-data/gbif-occurrences[BigQuery table^]. When using cloud-based snapshots, we always recommend creating a https://www.gbif.org/citation-guidelines#derivedDatasets[Derived Dataset citation^] for the records that you use. When referring to the full dataset, please use the appropriate citations as listed on the https://www.gbif.org/occurrence-snapshots[cloud-based datasets^] page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Target for macro image
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "intro-to-gbif::downloadoptions.png"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Cube*: An occurrence cube is a tab-separated csv file containing species occurrence measures (e.g. a count) summarized by taxonomic, temporal and/or spatial dimensions (e.g. a given year, a specific taxonomic rank, etc.).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:62
msgid "https://techdocs.gbif.org/en/data-use/download-formats[Occurrence download formats^] are fully documented in GBIF's technical documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "Handling data quality "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:68
msgid "Determining the precision and accuracy of the data for use is a key step in determining the usefulness of the data for any intended purpose.  While GBIF can support the identification of some quality issues that arise from within the data publishing workflow, handling some quality issues requires additional expert knowledge.  The two most common issues for which this may be required are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Data gaps* - sampling across taxonomic groups and geographic regions is not equal and users may need to take into account sampling bias in their analyses before the data can be used effectively. \n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Taxonomic misidentification* - some taxonomic groups may require additional information to ensure that taxa have been correctly identified such as images, videos and audio recordings that accompany data or collector information.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "*GBIF Flags for Data Quality Issues*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:75
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-publishing.adoc:222
msgid "https://techdocs.gbif.org/en/data-use/occurrence-issues-and-flags[Data quality issues and flags^] are documented in GBIF's technical documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:78
msgid "During the indexation process, GBIF assigns issues and flags to data for https://data-blog.gbif.org/post/issues-and-flags/[common data quality issues^].  These most frequently occur from data entry errors or missing data fields whose interpretation can be automated centrally by GBIF. These interpretations are classified as:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Excluded* - where the original data couldn’t be interpreted, so is excluded in the interpreted fields.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Altered* - where the original data is modified in the interpretation process to be indexed in GBIF.org.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Inferred* - where an empty field is inferred using other record information.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:84
msgid "Be aware that if you are filtering for data quality issues, you should reverse the filter to exclude those data that have been flagged with that issue. You can also see the verbatim data i.e. the non-interpreted data in a Darwin Core Archive if you would like to validate the interpretation process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "*How can I improve data quality?*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/intro-to-gbif/modules/ROOT/pages/data-access.adoc:90
msgid "Data publishers have the responsibility for improving the quality of the data, and as a user, you play a key role in identifying where there are errors.  If you should find an error in the data, you should contact the publisher directly using the contact details that GBIF provides on the publisher page.  GBIF also provides the ability for users to log data quality issues using the \"Feedback and questions\" button on the menu bar of http://www.gbif.org[GBIF.org^]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
